WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.864 --> 00:00:09.994
In this video, you'll see how Graduate Evidence helps you decide what to assign, based on which graduate attributes your class has practiced this year.

2
00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:20.725
Open your classroom and select the Assignments tab. At the top, you'll see Not sure what to assign? It's optional. Select Show me ideas if you'd like some.

3
00:00:21.227 --> 00:00:34.247
Fixer Nation picks a few games and lessons for your grade levels that would add practice for attributes your class hasn't practiced yet. Each one lists the attributes it adds. It's only a suggestion, and you choose.

4
00:00:34.748 --> 00:00:40.258
Select Assign on one you like. It joins your list below, and the ideas update.

5
00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:58.549
For the full picture, select See every attribute. Every attribute from New York's Social Emotional Learning Benchmarks and Portrait of a Graduate is listed, with how many of your students have practiced it. A student counts once they finish a lesson or game that Fixer Nation connects to that attribute.

6
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:09.020
The dark part of each bar is students who have practiced it. The light part is students who finished a related activity. It shows practice, not how well a student did.

7
00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:23.191
Some attributes say that no Fixer Nation activity is connected yet, or that only related ones are. Don't read that as zero. We just haven't connected an activity to it yet, so the page can't show practice for it.

8
00:01:23.692 --> 00:01:32.582
Administrators at your school see only counts for the whole school, never your students' names. Student names stay on your usual progress pages.
